    "narrative": "The centerpiece of the LawDog offensive engine today is undoubtedly **Bryce Harper**, who checks in with a 68.46 efficiency score against Scott. Batting third with the wind blowing out at his home park, **Bryce Harper** is positioned to maximize his xwOBA profile against a mid-tier starter. While our depth is thinned by the absence of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** on the IL, we are leaning heavily on **Masyn Winn** and **Luis Arraez** to anchor the batting average category. **Masyn Winn** provides the requisite stolen base floor that keeps us competitive in our scarcest category, and despite a neutral matchup, his volume at the top of the order keeps him as a \"Strong\" start. We are also closely tracking **Geraldo Perdomo**, whose sprint speed metrics make him an essential plugin for today\u2019s rotation, even as the optimizer balances his floor against tougher divisional arms.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Taylor Ward** versus **Gleyber Torres**. **Taylor Ward** narrowly missed the cut; while his power ceiling is high, the optimizer favored **Gleyber Torres** for his superior lineup stability and a favorable platoon matchup that mitigates the risk of a sub-40 efficiency floor. We are keeping **Lawrence Butler** and **Cal Raleigh** in reserve due to today\u2019s schedule, forcing us to rely on **Matt Chapman** and **JJ Bleday** to provide the necessary HR/RBI production to supplement **Bryce Harper**. Owners should monitor the weather reports for the **Jonathan Aranda** matchup, as any precipitation delays could impact the bullpen usage, potentially forcing us to utilize **Zack Gelof** or **Brendan Donovan** as a late-inning pivot if the game script shifts. We have effectively benched **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Yainer Diaz** to preserve our remaining game caps, ensuring our high-leverage assets are available for the weekend series.",
